# Repository-scoped npm configuration for the ArkCase frontend build.
#
# engine-strict turns the "engines" block of package.json ("node": ">=20.19.0 <21", "npm": ">=10")
# from advice into a precondition: npm's own default is engine-strict=false, under which an
# out-of-range runtime only prints an EBADENGINE warning and the install proceeds anyway, so a
# Node 6/8-era or Node 22+ runtime would still be able to produce a node_modules tree and a bundle -
# exactly the outcome the Node 20 migration exists to prevent. With it, npm refuses the install and
# exits non-zero, which is what makes the declared runtime enforceable rather than documentary.
#
# npm reads this file as project configuration for whichever project directory the install resolves
# to, so the same gate applies to every install path: a developer or CI run of `npm ci` /
# `npm install` from this folder, and the deploy-time `npm ci` that AngularResourceCopier runs in
# ~/.arkcase/tmp (this file is staged there through the filesToCopyFromArchive list in
# acm-user-interface/ark-angular-starter/src/main/resources/spring/spring-web-ark-angular-starter.xml).
#
# Deliberately NOT set here: ignore-scripts. Installs must pass --ignore-scripts on the command line
# (one git-sourced asset repository's prepare script tries to build an ancient native module), but
# setting it in this file would also suppress the "prebuild" hook of "npm run build" and the generated
# profiles module would never be written.
engine-strict=true
